        "original_id": "24e0c165-26e6-5de0-8f77-a93038089688",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Cullen, Paul Melba, Val Doonican\n- Products: Punchlines, Eye Guess, The Val Doonican Show\n- Topics: game show hosting, television appearances\n\nFacts:\n- Eye Guess was an American game show that originally ran from 1966 to 1969.\n- In 1979, a failed American game show pilot titled Punchlines was hosted by Bill Cullen and rebooted Eye Guess.\n- Bill Cullen became best known as a game show host, hosted 23 shows during his career, and was nicknamed the \"Dean of Game Show Hosts\".\n- Paul Melba appeared on television in Punchlines and in eight editions of The Val Doonican Show, in addition to appearing in clubs and theatres.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4dbddfa8-3612-5ced-99d9-c96daecd4371",
        "text": "Page: Punchlines. Sentence: The show itself was based on a failed 1979 American game show pilot of the same name hosted by Bill Cullen for which in turn was a reboot of another American game show from 1966-69 called \"Eye Guess\".\nPage: Bill Cullen. Sentence: His biggest claim to fame was as a game show host; over the course of his career, he hosted 23 shows, and earned the nickname \"Dean of Game Show Hosts\".\nPage: Paul Melba. Sentence: In addition to appearances in clubs and theatres he has made several other television appearances, including \"Punchlines\" and eight editions of \"The Val Doonican Show\".",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
